.TH SPACEGL-CLIENT 1 "2026-11-01" "SpaceGL @VERSION@" "SpaceGL Manual"
.SH NAME
spacegl-client \- SpaceGL tactical bridge launcher script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B spacegl-client
.RB [ \-\-no\-banner ]
.RI [ gl | vk ]
.RI [ "DECK OPTIONS" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B spacegl-client
starts the command deck,
.BR spacegl_client (1):
it shows the SpaceGL banner (on a terminal), makes sure a master key is
available, then replaces itself with the deck. Every argument except
.B \-\-no\-banner
is passed on unchanged; the exit status and the signals are the deck's
own, and the deck's standard input (the captain's answers) is not read
by the script. Pass
.B gl
for the OpenGL frontend or
.B vk
for the Vulkan frontend (GPU-driven rendering by default, with a
CPU-driven fallback;
.B SPACEGL_GPD=0
selects the CPU-driven path). The deck starts the viewer it finds as
.I ./build/spacegl_3dview
(or
.IR spacegl_vulkan ),
.I ./spacegl_3dview
or in
.BR PATH .
.PP
Server identity (wire revision 4): on the first connection to a server
the deck prints the server's fingerprint and pins its key in
.IR ~/.spacegl/known_servers .
Check it against the fingerprint the server prints at boot. A later
connection to the same address with another key is refused with
"SERVER IDENTITY CHANGED"; if the change is legitimate (the server's data
directory was replaced), remove that server's line from the file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-banner
No banner and no screen clearing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
The script's usage, then the deck's.
.PP
Every other option is the deck's (see
.BR spacegl_client (1)).
.SH MASTER KEY
The key is taken from the first source that exists:
.B SPACEGL_KEY_FILE
(a file of 64 hex digits, mode 0600),
.BR SPACEGL_KEY ,
.IR ~/.spacegl/key ;
the script names the source it found and the program reads it. Only when
none exists, and only on a terminal, the script asks for the key (not
echoed; 64 hex digits or at least 32 characters, three attempts) and
passes it in
.BR SPACEGL_KEY .
Without a terminal (a pipe, a service) nothing is asked and the program
creates
.IR ~/.spacegl/key .
.B \-\-help ,
.B \-\-version
and
.B \-\-print\-identity
show no banner and ask nothing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR SPACEGL_KEY_FILE ", " SPACEGL_KEY
The master key (see MASTER KEY).
.TP
.B SPACEGL_SERVER_KEY
The server's identity key (64 hex digits, from
.BR "spacegl-server \-\-print\-identity" ):
the deck accepts only a server that signs the handshake with it.
.TP
.B SPACEGL_KNOWN_SERVERS
Path of the known_servers file (default ~/.spacegl/known_servers).
.TP
.B SPACEGL_GPD
For the Vulkan frontend: unset or 1 GPU-driven (default), 0 CPU-driven.
.TP
.B SPACEGL_BIN_DIR
Directory of the program to run. Without it the script looks in the
build tree next to itself, in its own directory (an installed
.IR /usr/bin ),
in
.I ./build
and
.I .
of the current directory, then in
.BR PATH .
.TP
.B SPACEGL_NO_BANNER
1: no banner and no screen clearing (like
.BR \-\-no\-banner ).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Set: no colours (they are also off when the output is not a terminal).
.SH EXIT STATUS
The program's own (the script replaces itself with it);
.B 2
when no valid key was entered,
.B 127
when the program is not found.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.spacegl/known_servers
The pinned identity of every server this deck has met.
.TP
.I ~/.spacegl/key
The default master key.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spacegl_client (1),
.BR spacegl-server (1),
.BR spacegl_vulkan (1),
.BR spacegl_3dview (1)
